{
  "_comment": [
    "The detect-001 golden set. AI spec §7.2.",
    "",
    "Fifteen hand-labelled AMBIGUOUS systems, three per archetype. Each case is",
    "recorded as EVIDENCE rather than as a tree, and that is deliberate: the pass",
    "only ever sees scores, rule names, paths and a bounded listing (AI spec §4",
    "step 4), so evidence is the whole input. Recording trees instead would make",
    "the eval inputs a function of the detector's current scoring, and a change to",
    "a rule weight would silently change what the golden set measures.",
    "",
    "`archetype` is the HAND LABEL -- what a human who looked at the real system",
    "concluded. It is the truth the report scores `primary` against; it is not what",
    "the heuristics said, which is the point of the case being here at all.",
    "",
    "Every case is ambiguous by construction: no archetype's score clears",
    "DETECT_CONFIDENCE_MIN, which is the only situation in which this prompt is",
    "ever called.",
    "",
    "`listing` entries are anonymized: real client paths never enter this",
    "repository, and a golden set that carried them would put client structure in",
    "an Apache-2.0 tree permanently."
  ],
